From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:26:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: use the S_PARM frame rate for HEVC rate
 control
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The other encoders program E_RC_FRAME_RATE from the frame rate set with
VIDIOC_S_PARM. HEVC only uses the control
V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEVC_FRAME_RATE_RESOLUTION, which defaults to 1. So
with frame rate control on, the firmware spreads the bitrate over one
frame per second: on the Pixel 7 (MFC v15), 4 Mbit/s asked at 30 fps
gave about 18 Mbit/s.

Use the S_PARM frame rate when it is set, and the HEVC control otherwise.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c    | 16 +++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
index 3f1e6e694..97fba11ac 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
@@ -1755,13 +1755,19 @@ static int s5p_mfc_set_enc_params_hevc(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx)
 	reg |= p_hevc->rc_frame_qp;
 	writel(reg, mfc_regs->e_rc_config);
 
-	/* frame rate */
+	/*
+	 * frame rate: the one set with S_PARM, as for the other codecs, or
+	 * else the HEVC frame rate control (1 fps by default)
+	 */
 	if (p->rc_frame) {
 		reg = 0;
-		reg &= ~(0xFFFF << 16);
-		reg |= ((p_hevc->rc_framerate) << 16);
-		reg &= ~(0xFFFF);
-		reg |= FRAME_DELTA_DEFAULT;
+		if (p->rc_framerate_num && p->rc_framerate_denom) {
+			reg |= ((p->rc_framerate_num & 0xFFFF) << 16);
+			reg |= p->rc_framerate_denom & 0xFFFF;
+		} else {
+			reg |= ((p_hevc->rc_framerate) << 16);
+			reg |= FRAME_DELTA_DEFAULT;
+		}
 		writel(reg, mfc_regs->e_rc_frame_rate);
 	}
 
